},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"With ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximumCardinality","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the heaviest among the maximum-cardinality matchings; without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, a negative edge is never taken and a zero-weight one may be. Among parallel edges, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"heaviest copy is used (the earliest on ties). Self-loops are never weighed; ","type":"text"},{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"called once per other edge, in position order. Integer arithmetic is exact.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n³)."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside"},{"name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every |weight| ≤ "},{"code":"W.max \/ 8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and n · |weight| ≤ "},{"code":"W.max \/ 8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"maximumCardinality","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (its duals go negative, by up to about n times the greatest weight);"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the total weight fits in "},{"code":"W","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Beyond that, arithmetic may overflow, which traps."}]}],"style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/matchingmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumweightmatching(weight:maximumcardinality:)-6l4u0"]}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edges-swift.associatedtype","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"assoc